            "content_alignment": "left",
            "subheading": "",
            "heading": "Challenge",
            "highlight_style": "none",
            "highlight_font_style": "italic",
            "highlight_style_color": "",
            "highlight_text_color": "",
            "heading_size": "h2",
            "description": "<p> The labels weren’t merely for branding; they also had to incorporate crucial care and usage instructions for each cover type. Although sourcing labels overseas was an option, Shehwen feared potential compromises in quality and logistical hurdles.<br/><br/>Moreover, because Cover Express prioritized catering to individuals with specific mobility needs, they soon garnered the attention of the Veterans Administration. However, to onboard the VA as a customer, both the products and labels needed to be 100% American-made.<br/><br/>This posed an additional obstacle in acquiring customized, high-quality, and cost-effective labels manufactured domestically.<br/><br/></p>",
            "text_size": "text-base",
